# Restart drain

**Invariant:** `needed(restart) ⇒ fire(restart)` — busy, in-flight, a peer's stream, a dirty tree, an open
Cowork tab, or "this IDE session" is never a reason to skip, park.
`edit(served_path ∨ env_loaded_by_process) ∧ running(process) ⇒ recycle(process)` same turn; `bind_mount ⇏ live`.
That recycle is **not** a work-complete claim.

No service is forced by default (K48). Busy G1 ⇒ wait for the drain. A force needs a coordinator force_reason announced to Kaywan or maestro first; manage refuses caller force over busy G1 without one (409); mcp force is allowed only when busy is life_hot only (a:39670).
`git_integration_worker`: arm drain (`status=deferred`, `restart_intent_id`) — never force, never kill. Live cursor-sdk dispatch ⇒ park, not wait (`park_live=true`). `recycle_giw` is park-first at idle; force only on CANCEL_FAILED / NEST_CHAIN / STATE_ROOT_MISSING.

## Forbidden / Required

`pkill` / `kill` / `docker stop` for lifecycle is forbidden — use `manage(action="sync_restart"|"restart"|"stop")`.
Do not poll `wait_healthy` in-window while holding the write lease — arm, **exit**, probe later.
Do not claim `live` from a commit, an import, or `status=deferred` — process start after served-file **and** env mtime, or a live probe.
Do not report exact `live@<sha>` when served dirt was loaded — report `live` + tree state; `live@<sha>` needs path-explicit commit **before** restart.
Do not hold graph stamps / todo close for `live@sha` — close once ACs met and ordinary `live` proven (or `liveness n/a`).
Do not recycle-as-finished while session paths are uncommitted — commit session paths, **then** recycle; quote both payloads.

## Go-live = work-complete finishing (last)

Default (not a strategy choice):

```
land the work → path-explicit commit of session paths → recycle serving processes
```

`work_complete ⇒ commit(path-explicit, session_paths) ≺ recycle(every serving process) ∧ stamp(graph)`.
"Go live / activate / everything live?" are that contract, not a second permission gate.
`live@sha` is already this order. **Recycle-from-dirty-tree is retired as the ordinary-live default.**
Exceptional mid-arc verify (bind-mount / `docker cp`): mark exceptional and commit session paths
**before any done claim** — not a next-turn sequel. `needed(restart)` mid-arc is not finishing.

`work_complete` ∉ L(x) without quoted commit + recycle payloads. Fluency ≠ the act. Trust tool payloads.

"Only create commits when requested" = opportunistic/unrelated commits; **not** a veto of this
contract. The seat commits session paths without asking. Checkpoint commit and `/session-end`
are not work-complete.

Restart-after-land is the default. Gateway GPU pre-check withholds a gateway stop when the socket is missing or uncheckable (not a busy-skip).
